      "width": 800,
      "height": 600,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "InSapphoWeTrust from Los Angeles, California, USA",
      "description": "The village down there was formed to serve the visitors and tourists to Bulguksa.\n\nI am up the hill in the parking lot for Seokguram, a Buddhist grotto. From Bulguksa to Seokguram, it is a 2.5-kilometer (1.5-mile) hike, or 50 minutes, on foot, or a 8-kilometer (5-mile) drive, or 20 minutes, by car. I chose to drive the very crooked road up from Bulguksa, testing the cornering abilities of the Sonata; even though it wasn't as sharp as the BMW 3-series I was driving back in the US at the time (I was looking to sell it immediately upon my US return, however), it was more than adequate.",
      "dateCreated": "2008-11-17 11:47",
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "bulguksa-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "wy7g",
